<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Latin America</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> America is the region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a> where Romance languages, chiefly Spanish and Portuguese, predominate. It was shaped by the colonial rule of the Spanish and Portuguese empires, which transformed its religion, languages and societies. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a> was one of the most stable states in nineteenth-century Latin America.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/latin-america.jpg" alt="Latin America" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heraldry · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Latin_America_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
